From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:19:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/79] server: the in-thinking runner through the chat route,
 on C3's owned span

The server side of the in-model runner (slice 5 of C4), on top of C3
(merged in from a parallel branch: no file is shared with slices 1-4).

- runner_guide.zig and RUNNER-GUIDE.md: PREFIX_GUIDE's default guide in a
  chat's system message, a request's own "runner_guide", and runner_trace*
  checks; compute_turns.guideAsked keeps the compute default's rule.
- runner_text.zig: the server gives the runner its tokenizer at start.
- runner_commit_ask.zig: PREFIX_COMMIT's request settings (Request.run_commit).
- chat.prepare sets run_cells, think_end, run_trace and run_commit when the
  engine serves a runner (Info.runner).
- Mailbox keeps the runner's records (Event.cells) and receipt; Generation
  streams the records the client has (tensorfold.runner.cells), sets C3's
  Generation.owned from reply_owned.of over the cell writes, and puts the
  runner receipt and guide hash in the reply's runtime.
- runner_projection.zig: abstain anchors mapped onto the fields the client got
  (openai.zig's Run.sent); tool_parse's Envelope and envelopes are now pub.
- openai passes the runner fields through; compute segments count the tokens
  before them (Generation.base) for the records.
- DeepSeek-V4.1's serve engine opens the runner through runner_binding.dsv41:
  TF_RUNNER=1 or TF_DSV41_RUNNER=1, as before; Flash-Next stays unbound.
- test-runner-server-host: the guide, commit ask, projection and live-record
  tests.

Ported from the dsv41 release line (s86 7b79ef92d); runner_owned.zig is not
ported again (C3's reply_owned.zig). The DSV41 runner round trace waits for
lanes' round_trace (slice 6).
